# Working notes behind scripts/roadmap/. The roadmap data and the pages generated from
# it are fine in public — they are the same kind of thing as the issue list. These two
# are not: they carry a private read of the national federation's internal position,
# taken from a conversation with one of its officers, and a description of a specific
# supporter that identifies him to anyone in Dutch photo-club circles. Neither belongs
# in a public repository. Kept locally because they are still being worked on.
# Extended from notes-*.md to notes-*: working material also arrives as CSV, such as a
# scrape of another organisation's public club roster, which is ours to use but not to
# republish wholesale.
scripts/roadmap/notes-*

# Ratings exported from the roadmap page (scripts/roadmap). A transient hand-off file:
# build-roadmap.py merges it into feature-candidates.csv, which is the master and is
# committed. Keeping the export as well would mean the same numbers in two places, and
# churn on every rating session.
scripts/roadmap/ratings.csv
